• microwaves are transverse; sound are longitudinal;
• microwaves have higher frequency (than sound);
• microwaves can be polarised but sound can’t;
• microwaves can travel through a vacuum but sound can’t/requires a medium OR sound are mechanical waves but microwaves are EM waves
Also accept: weak descriptions in terms of parallel and perpendicular oscillations/vibrations with direction of energy transfer.
Not accepted: reference to applications e.g. cooking food.
